==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|throwen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|þrāwen}}, {{m|ang|ġeþrāwen}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*þrēanaz}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*þrēaną}}. {{doublet|en|thran}}.

Morphologically {{suffix|en|throw|n<id:past participle>}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|thrōn|a=RP}}, {{IPA|en|/θɹəʊn/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Pvanp7-thrown.wav|a=UK}}
** {{audio|en|En-uk-thrown.ogg|a=UK}}
* {{enPR|thrōn|a=GA}}, {{IPA|en|/θɹoʊn/}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-thrown.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|əʊn|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|throne}}

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{past participle of|en|throw}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Launched by throwing.
#: {{co|en|a '''thrown''' weapon}}
# Twisted into a single thread, as silk or yarn.
# {{lb|en|slang}} Confused; perplexed.
#: {{ux|en|I was totally '''thrown''' by his bizarre remarks.}}

